sed": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`llm logs` now shows server-executed tool results. The check from the spec passes: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_llm_logs.py tests/test_plugins.py` gives 93 passed. I ran only that command, not the full suite.\n\nI read the implementer's diff and it matches the spec:\n\n- **`llm/logs.py`**:\n  - `_LogRowBuilder` has the new `_output_segment_hashes` method and sets `_output_message_hashes` on each row.\n  - `log_row_extras` takes tool call ids and server result ids from the output messages.\n  - `log_row_extras` adds `server_executed` to every tool call and tool result, right after `exception` in results.\n  - Server results are collected from the output parts, after the local ones from the input parts.\n- **`llm/cli.py`**:\n  - `_output_message_hashes` is stripped in `annotate_log_rows`.\n  - The result-printing loop is now a nested `_display_tool_results` helper.\n  - The prompt section prints only local results, and server results print under the response, after `### Tool calls` and before the response text.\n- **`docs/changelog.md`**: the #1629 bullet is added under the unreleased section. It says `--short` where the spec said `--short` with backticks and `llm logs`, so the wording is slightly adjusted.", "ttft_ms": 1459, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 24387, "uuid": "6cddbe92-49d3-432a-8b8c-ee7a4f94bc5a", "ttft_stream_ms": 1075, "time_to_request_ms": 15, "first_content_frame_ms": 1075, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
